        <td>Limited</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Wave</strong></td>
        <td>Free</td>
        <td>Good</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>No</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>YNAB</strong></td>
        <td>$15/mo</td>
        <td>No</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>No</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Zoho Expense</strong></td>
        <td>Free/$4+</td>
        <td>Good</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Shoeboxed</strong></td>
        <td>$18/mo</td>
        <td>Excellent</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>No</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><strong>Rydoo</strong></td>
        <td>$10/mo</td>
        <td>Excellent</td>
        <td>Excellent</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
        <td>Yes</td>
      </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="receipt-scanning">Receipt Scanning Accuracy</h2>

  <p>
    Receipt scanning uses OCR to extract data. Quality varies significantly.
  </p>

  <h3>Best Receipt Scanning</h3>
  <p>
    Expensify SmartScan is human-verified for accuracy and handles handwritten receipts. Shoeboxed
    offers human verification and is excellent for faded receipts. Rydoo uses AI and handles
    multiple languages well.
  </p>

  <h3>Tips for Better Scans</h3>
  <p>
    Photograph in good lighting with receipt flat. Capture the entire receipt including date and
    total. Scan immediately because thermal paper fades quickly. Add notes for unclear items while
    you remember.
  </p>

  <h2 id="multi-currency">Multi-Currency for Nomads</h2>

  <p>
    Digital nomads deal with multiple currencies constantly. Best expense apps handle this.
  </p>

  <h3>Automatic Currency Conversion</h3>
  <p>
    Expensify converts at date-of-purchase exchange rate. Rydoo offers real-time rates with
    automatic conversion. Wave handles multi-currency accounts and transactions. YNAB does
    multi-currency budgets and tracking.
  </p>

  <h3>Tax Reporting in Home Currency</h3>
  <p>
    You'll report all income and expenses in your home currency for taxes. Make sure your app
    exports reports in a single currency with proper exchange rate documentation.
  </p>

  <h2 id="integrations">Integrations</h2>

  <p>
    Your expense tracker should sync with accounting software to avoid double entry.
  </p>

  <h3>QuickBooks Integration</h3>
  <p>
    Expensify and Zoho Expense and Shoeboxed all sync directly. QuickBooks Self-Employed is built
    in.
  </p>

  <h3>Xero Integration</h3>
  <p>
    Expensify and Zoho Expense and Rydoo all integrate. Receipt Bank which is now Dext is popular
    with Xero users.
  </p>

  <h3>FreshBooks Integration</h3>
  <p>
    Built-in expense tracking is solid. <a href="/tools/best-accounting-software-freelancers">Expensify integration
    available</a>.
  </p>

  <h2 id="faq">Questions</h2>

  <FAQSection faqs={faqData}/>

  <h2>Recommendations</h2>

  <p>
    Best overall. Expensify for best receipt scanning and multi-currency and integrations.
  </p>

  <p>
    Best for tax. QuickBooks Self-Employed for expense tracking plus tax estimates.
  </p>

  <p>
    Best free. Wave for full features at no cost.
  </p>

  <p>
    Best for nomads. Rydoo for multi-currency and travel focus and per diems.
  </p>

  <p>
    Best for budgeting. YNAB to control spending not just track it.
  </p>

  <p>
    Start tracking today. Every expense you capture is a potential tax deduction. The savings
    compound throughout the year.
  </p>

  <Fragment slot="full-width">
    <RelatedArticles articles={relatedArticles}/>
  </Fragment>
</ArticleLayout>
